          { name: "Assuming Renter Disengagement & Ignoring Housing Affordability", tag: "avoid", why: "With a 34.6% renter rate in a district with $87,837 median income, FL-HD-16 has a significant population of young professionals and smaller households for whom housing costs represent a material burden relative to income. Treating renters as politically marginal or assuming they are satisfied with current housing policy is a strategic error — younger renters and professionals navigating Florida's housing market are acutely aware of affordability constraints and are evaluating candidates on whether government is addressing supply, zoning, and housing cost growth. Any candidate who ignores the renter constituency's housing affordability concerns in a district where one-third of households rent is leaving a mobilizable opposition constituency untended." }
