          "Map the 3.4% demographic gap and conduct targeted outreach to the likely additional minority residents it represents; assuming the 16.21% Hispanic figure is complete understates the actual minority constituency and creates blind spots in constituent service and campaign messaging.",
          "Address wage-level job creation and workforce development directly; the 17.9% college attainment rate signals a constituency that relies on high-school-credential employment, making local economic development and wage standards material voting concerns rather than secondary issues.",
          "Treat the 35% opposition not as noise but as a baseline that could expand if economic messaging shifts or turnout among renters and minority voters increases; in a district with this income profile and demographic complexity, a 65-35 margin is not a permanent coalition but a current snapshot dependent on continued alignment."
