          { name: "Assuming Demographic Stability in an Aging District", tag: "avoid", why: "At 57.0-year median age, FL-HD-76 is aging and will continue aging; the Hispanic population at 15.46% is substantially lower than statewide trends and may grow. A 71-point margin that rests entirely on an aging white homeowner base, without active coalition maintenance among younger and minority voters, creates a pathway to competitive redistricting or demographic-driven margin compression within two election cycles. Complacency about demography in a rapidly changing state is the highest-risk strategic error in this district." }
