          "FL-HD-84 is a solidly Republican district in electoral terms—Trabulsy's 58-42 win in 2024 is a comfortable margin—but the underlying demographic profile reveals a constituency under genuine economic stress. The median household income of $61,937 is only modestly above the national median, the median age of 47.3 is in the older-worker range where fixed costs (healthcare, property taxes, home maintenance) rise faster than incomes, and college attainment at 25.1% signals a working- and middle-class constituency without the educational credentials that typically insulate households from wage stagnation. The 26.2% renter rate indicates a meaningful non-homeowner population that often experiences housing cost burden acutely. This is not a wealthy Republican base consolidating gains—it is an older, education-constrained, income-modest constituency whose 58% Republican lean reflects current representation and incumbent performance, not an immovable partisan preference. A challenger who offers concrete answers to the material concerns of households at this income and age intersection—healthcare affordability, property tax fairness, housing costs, and job quality—has real opening here.",
