          { name: "Cultural Conservatism as a Unifying Message", tag: "avoid", why: "While national-origin cohorts within the Latino community (Cuban-heritage, Venezuelan, and others) have demonstrated cultural conservative voting patterns, FL-HD-115's high income and education level create a constituency evaluating candidates on economic and governance performance first. Messaging that prioritizes cultural conservatism or anti-woke positioning at the expense of addressing healthcare affordability, education quality, housing costs, and small business support will underperform with college-educated, professionally employed Latino voters in a district this affluent—and will repel the 34% renter population whose economic concerns may differ substantially from homeowner-majority priorities." }
